{title: My Help Comes from the Lord}
{subtitle: Psalm 121}
{key: Cm}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Cm] | [Cm] | [Cm] | [Cm] |
| [Cm] | [Cm] | [Cm] | [Bb] |
| [Cm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I lift up my eyes to [Bb]the moun[Ab]tains
Where does [Bb]my help [Cm]come from
My help comes from [Bb]the Lord
[Ab]Who made [Bb]heaven and [Cm]earth
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Ab]He who [Bb]keeps you will not [Cm]slumber
[Ab]He [Bb]who keeps Israel will [G]not sleep
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Cm]The Lord is your keeper
[Bb]The Lord is your shade at your right [Ab]hand
The [Cm]sun shall not strike you by [Bb]day
Nor the [Ab]moon [Bb]by [Cm]night
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Ab]He who [Bb]keeps you will not [Cm]slumber
[Ab]He who [Bb]keeps Israel will not [G]sleep
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
From [Cm]this time [Bb]forth and fo[Ab]revermore
{end_of_verse}
